    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This 11-day Silk Road Xinjiang tour takes you from the legendary Sunday Market of Kashgar, through the vast deserts of Xinjiang, to the ancient Mogao Caves of Dunhuang, and finally to the Terracotta Warriors in Xi'an. Travel with a private English-speaking guide, stay in comfortable 4-star hotels, and experience the very best of the ancient Silk Road across western China.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Explore Kashgar's vibrant Sunday Market</li><li>Drive the spectacular Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</li>
      <li>Visit Karakul Lake with views of Muztagh Ata</li><li>Discover the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li>
      <li>Camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes</li><li>Walk the Jiayuguan Fortress</li><li>Marvel at the Terracotta Warriors in Xi'an</li><li>Cycle the ancient Xi'an City Wall</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Kashgar</h4><p>Arrive at Kashgar Airport. Your guide will meet you and transfer to your hotel. Free time to explore the Old City and sample authentic Uyghur cuisine.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Kashgar 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar —Sunday Market & Old City</h4><p>Experience the legendary Kashgar Sunday Market, a centuries-old trading hub. Visit the Id Kah Mosque, the largest in China, and wander through the maze-like alleys of the Old City. Afternoon visit to Abakh Khoja Tomb.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Kashgar 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar —Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</h4><p>Drive along the breathtaking Karakoram Highway. Visit Karakul Lake at 3,600m, with panoramic views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m). Arrive in Taxkorgan, China's westernmost town, surrounded by the Pamir Mountains.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Taxkorgan 3★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Taxkorgan 鈫?Kashgar 鉁?Urumqi</h4><p>Morning visit to the ancient Stone Fort and grasslands. Return to Kashgar via the Karakoram Highway. Evening flight to Urumqi, capital of Xinjiang.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Urumqi 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi 鈫?Turpan</h4><p>Drive to Turpan (3 hours), the second-lowest depression on Earth. Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins and the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system. Experience the unique grape culture of the Turpan Basin.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Turpan 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan 鈫?Dunhuang</h4><p>Morning visit to the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley. Afternoon high-speed train to Dunhuang (approx. 4 hours), the gateway to the Mogao Caves.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Dunhuang 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang —Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full UNESCO day. Morning at the Mogao Caves, a millennium of Buddhist art carved into desert cliffs. Afternoon camel ride and sand surfing at the Singing Sand Dunes. Sunset at Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Dunhuang 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang 鈫?Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive to Jiayuguan (5 hours) through the vast Gobi Desert. Visit the Jiayuguan Fortress —the western terminus of the Great Wall of China, standing guard at the edge of the desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Jiayuguan 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan 鉁?Xi'an</h4><p>Morning visit to the Overhanging Great Wall. Fly to Xi'an, the ancient capital where the Silk Road began. Evening stroll through the Muslim Quarter, sampling local street food.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Xi'an 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an —Terracotta Warriors & City Wall</h4><p>Morning visit to the Army of Terracotta Warriors —one of the world's greatest archaeological discoveries. Afternoon cycling on the ancient City Wall, offering panoramic views of Xi'an.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃彣 Xi'an 4★?/span><span>馃嵔 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Xi'an</h4><p>Free time until your airport transfer. Your Silk Road adventure concludes in the ancient capital. 鍐嶈�!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>馃嵔 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

